# WENGE-0010 / SPEC-0001 O10, and the review checklist rule "every NoteOn has velocity at
# least 1". Ref: CE v5.30 p.40, Step Event Consideration 1: "If the Velocity is 0 then the
# note is not transmitted." A MIDI NoteOn with velocity 0 is a NoteOff to every receiver, so
# neither a NoteOn nor a NoteOff is sent. The lowest velocity that sounds is 1.
seed 1
bpm 120
page.tracks 0,1 enabled
track 0 vel 0
track 1 vel 1
track 0 mch 1
track 1 mch 2
play
# One bar is 96,000 samples at 120 BPM (500 samples a tick, D0: the manual's 192 ticks to the
# whole note), and a step is 6,000, so 40 buffers of 512 (20,480 samples) hold exactly one
# firing and its NoteOff.
render 40 buffers buffer=512
expect event on ch=1 absent
expect event off ch=1 absent
expect event on ch=2 vel=1 count=1
expect event on vel=0 absent
expect balance
